# Exo Free — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: OpenCode Zen (`opencode/exo-free`; anonymous free stealth slot; **no AA page (404) / no vendor ever named / no model card / no published benchmark**)
- Date: 2026-11-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Verdict — SELF-EXCLUDED.** **Exo Free** is **not a scoreable artifact**. It was an **anonymous, limited-time free "stealth" slot on OpenCode Zen** — surfaced to the community only as *"the newly released anonymous model 'Exo'"* — that **lived roughly three days in early October 2026 before being pulled**, and today answers **HTTP 410 `ModelDeprecated`** while the catalog still carries it as `status:"active"`. The curated `meta` states it outright: *"An unidentified vendor's free OpenCode Zen stealth slot … no vendor, no card, no benchmarks … the folder's findings are a self-exclusion."* Scoring is impossible because **(a) there is no named vendor or model card — nothing identifies what 'Exo' actually was**; **(b) it has zero independent measurement — Artificial Analysis returns 404 (no Intelligence Index / Speed / Cost)**; and **(c) not a single benchmark was ever published under the `exo-free` label.** The community's only substantive observations were structural (1M ctx / 131K out, image-in, `variants:["high"]`, reasoning-only, free) and speculative about its backend (*"another router?", "might be a Gemini model?"*). Any score would require **inventing numbers or re-crediting a guessed backend** — so the entry is excluded, not scored.

## Why this is a self-exclusion (not a scored model)

- **Anonymous stealth slot with no vendor identity.** OpenCode issue **#54065** (*"Model exo-free has been deprecated,"* opened 2026-10-09, reproduced by the OpenCode agent on 2.0.26) describes it as *"the newly released anonymous model 'Exo'"*. No upstream lab, license, Hugging Face repo, or model card was ever attached to the name. Zen maintainer `rekram1-node` closed it as a routine free-tier sunset — *"Free models run for a limited time, the model wasn't correctly updated in models.dev to say deprecated — fixed"* — confirming it was a transient promotional slot, not a documented model.
- **Zero published benchmarks, and no independent tracker coverage.** **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/exo-free` → 404** (no Intelligence Index, no Speed, no Cost). No leaderboard cell, provider evaluation, or hands-on score exists under the `exo-free` label anywhere. The only catalog data is structural: `{ id:"opencode/exo-free", name:"Exo Free", released: 1791244800000, variants:["high"], cost:[{input:0,output:0,cache:{read:0,write:0}}], status:"active" }` — pricing/spec fields, **not capability measurements**.
- **The catalog/server mismatch shows a dead slot, not a live model.** The Zen `/models` list kept returning `exo-free` with `status:"active"`, while the inference endpoint answered **HTTP 410 `ModelDeprecated`** on every chat completion (reproduced 2026-10-11 and 2026-10-12/14). Because `exo-free` was, briefly, the **default model for fresh installs**, every new user's first prompt failed — a lifecycle bug on a retired slot, not evidence of a working, benchmarkable model.
- **Backend identity is speculation, not attribution.** Community threads asked whether Exo was *"another router"* or *"a Gemini model? (Probably…)"* — explicitly **unconfirmed guesses**. Attributing any specific vendor's scores to `exo-free` would be **fabricated reattribution**, the exact failure the corpus guards against.

## What we did establish (documented, not scored)

- **Real lifecycle facts (from #54065 + Zen catalog + Reddit):** listed on OpenCode Zen as `exo-free` in early Oct 2026 (catalog `released` epoch ≈ 2026-10-02; community "New Stealth Model" post ≈ 2026-10-06), **free $0/$0/$0**, **1,048,576 ctx / 131,072 max output**, **text + image in → text out**, reasoning exposed only as **`variants:["high"]`**, was the **fresh-install default model** for a period, then **deprecated within ~3 days** and now returns **410**.
- **Pattern match:** this is the **anonymous OpenCode Zen stealth-slot** family — the same reasoning used to exclude **`big-pickle`** (rotating stealth slot, "ground truth may never arrive"), **`owl-alpha`** (revealed alias whose only data belonged to an already-scored base), and **`ling-3.0-flash-sante`** (hosted-only variant with no own measurement). Like **`ox-alpha`** (documented as *"a third-party lab serving a reasoning model through OpenCode … without putting its name on the card"*), Exo's vendor was never identified — but unlike `ox-alpha`/`omen-alpha`, **Exo has no snapshot score or hands-on quantitative data at all**, only structural spec fields.

> **Consistency check:** an anonymous slot with **no vendor, no card, no AA page, and zero published numbers** cannot be scored without inventing data or guessing a backend. **No dimension scores are assigned.**

