- Method: public internet research (**Artificial Analysis `exo-free` → 404** (no independent measurement); **OpenCode GitHub issue #54065** *"Model exo-free has been deprecated"* — anonymous model 'Exo', HTTP 410 `ModelDeprecated`, catalog `variants:["high"]` / cost $0/$0/$0 / `status:"active"`, was the fresh-install default, closed as a limited-time free-tier sunset; **Reddit r/opencode** — "Exo Free (New Stealth Model)" + "exo free has been deprecated" threads; **developersdigest Ox Alpha guide** — corroborating anonymous-stealth-slot pattern ("third-party lab … without putting its name on the card"); **themodelgap / opencode changelog** — listed on Zen ~2026-10-06, usage attributed to "an unknown provider". **Curated `meta`** explicitly declares the folder's findings a self-exclusion: "no vendor, no card, no benchmarks.")
- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** a vendor **claims the Exo slot with a dated model card and its own published evaluation**, or a tracker (**Artificial Analysis / Vals / a hands-on leader**) measures an artifact under the `exo-free`/`Exo` name. **Guards applied:** (1) do **NOT** invent scores from the structural spec fields (1M ctx / $0 / `variants:["high"]`) — those are not capability measurements; (2) do **NOT** reattribute any candidate backend's benchmarks (Gemini / any router) onto Exo — the vendor was never identified and every "it's a Gemini model" claim is speculation; (3) do **NOT** treat the catalog's `status:"active"` as proof of a live, callable model — the endpoint returns 410; (4) **`ox-alpha`**/**`omen-alpha`**/**`big-pickle`** are separate stealth entries, not this one. **No dimension scores are assigned.**
